Kept: src/, configs_3b/, configs_7b/, inference_cli.py, pos_emb.pt,
neg_emb.pt, LICENSE. Left out: the ComfyUI node registration (__init__.py),
docs/, example_workflows/.

Changed by Parallx, in inference_cli.py, each marked with "Parallx:":
- reading an image: cv2.imdecode(np.fromfile(...)) instead of cv2.imread
- writing an image: cv2.imencode(...).tofile(...) instead of cv2.imwrite
Both because OpenCV's imread and imwrite fail on Windows when the path has a
character outside ASCII (a user folder named "José", for instance).

Parallx runs it through ../enhance.py, in a runtime the app installs
(docs/ENHANCE.md). Its own model download is never reached: the runtime
fetches and checks the model files first.
